<article class="env-lemma" id="08Q1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08Q1">Lemma <span data-tag="08Q1">10.134.3</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a polynomial algebra. Then $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}$ is homotopy equivalent to the chain complex $(0 \to \Omega _{B/A})$ with $\Omega _{B/A}$ in degree $0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/00S1" data-tag="00S1">10.134.2</a> and the fact that $\text{id}_ B : B \to B$ is a presentation of $B$ over $A$ with zero kernel. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>